 <p>
    Make sure you are following the homework expectations!
    Example: complete sentences!
  </p>

  <exercise>
    <introduction>
      <p>
        Grinnell Glacier in Glacier National Park in Montana covered about <m>142</m> 
        acres in 2007 
      and was found to be shrinking at a rate of <m>4.4\%</m> per year. Let <m>A(t)</m> denote the area of the Grinnell Glacier in acres in year <m>t</m>, 
        where <m>t</m> is the number of years since 2007.
      </p>
    </introduction>

    <task workspace="0.3in">
      <statement>
        <p>
            Find <m>A(0)</m>, <m>A(1)</m>, 
        and <m>A(2)</m>, carefully showing your calculations, and writing a sentence 
        (including units) for what each value means.
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>

    <task  workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          Find an exponential equation of the form <m>A(t) = ab^t</m> to model the number 
        of acres of ice in the Grinnell Glacier <m>t</m> years after 2007. Make it clear 
        what the final equation is, and explain your reasoning.
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>

    <task workspace=".5in">
      <statement>
        <p>
         How many acres of ice were in the glacier in 1997? In 2012? What does the model 
        predict for 2022? Carefully show your calculations. ("In 1997 there were .... In 2012 ....")
        </p>

      </statement>
    </task>

    <task workspace=".5in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          How many total acres of ice were lost from 2007 to 2012? Carefully show your calculations.
        </p>

       
      </statement>
    </task>

    <task workspace=".5in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          What was the average rate of change of <m>A</m> from 2007 to 2012? Carefully show 
        your calculations and write a sentence to explain the meaning of this number 
        and include units on your answer.
        </p>

        
      </statement>
    </task>

    <task workspace=".5in">
      <statement>
        <p>
         What was the average rate of change from 2012 to 2017? How does it compare to 
        the average rate of change from 2007 to 2012?
        </p>

      
      </statement>
    </task>

    <task workspace="0.5in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          When does the model predict the total number of acres 
          will be less than <m>60</m>? 
        Use Desmos, describing how you did so.
        </p>

       
      </statement>
    </task>

    
  </exercise>
</worksheet>